1
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:05,390
Yhibi-Oh!

2
00:00:05,473 --> 00:00:08,040
Yamu, Yamu, Yamu,

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,010
Yamu

4
00:00:09,093 --> 00:00:15,177
Yamu

5
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,100
Yu-Gi-Oh!

6
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,250
King прибils

7
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:06,617
Mokuba, how can you still
be on your brother's side?

8
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,876
He betrayed you to control Kaibokorn.

9
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:11,569
I would stand by my
brother no matter what.

10
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:14,337
We're family, and nothing's
going to separate us.

11
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:15,560
I don't believe it.

12
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:16,838
This is ridiculous.

13
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:20,037
Even after everything I've
shown him from his past,

14
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:24,837
all of those times Seto mistreated him,
and he's still being loyal to his brother.

15
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:28,685
I'm sick of Seto getting everything
and leaving me with nothing.

16
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:31,000
I deserve to have what he has.

17
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:33,640
And I'll start with his little brother.

18
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:38,540
From now on, I'll make sure that
Mokuba is loyal to me instead of Seto.

19
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:44,180
I'll crush him by taking the one thing he
thought he'd never lose, Mokuba's trust.

20
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:48,020
What do you think your brother's
thinking right now? Huh?

21
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,457
Tell me, do you honestly believe
your brother is coming to rescue you?

22
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:55,658
Or is he glad you're out of
his way once and for all?

23
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:58,277
Seto's definitely coming here to get me.

24
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,440
And when he does, you'll be sorry.

25
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,940
Is that right?

26
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:06,260
Well, why don't you ask him yourself,
because he's right behind you.

27
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,680
Huh? Seto!

28
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:12,000
That was fast.

29
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:13,611
I knew you'd come get me.

30
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,800
Don't take another step, Mokuba.

31
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:18,577
Why don't you take a
seat, you little brat?

32
00:02:18,660 --> 00:02:22,220
I'm sick and tired of you
always holding me back, Mokuba.

33
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:25,060
It's your fault we're still stuck here.

34
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:26,490
Seto, no!

35
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:27,640
Get a life.

36
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:32,600
Please come back! Seto!

37
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:35,920
You can't leave me here with him!

38
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,360
Seto, what happened?

39
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:40,140
What did I tell you?

40
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:46,867
It looks to me like your so-called brother
couldn't care less where you end up.

41
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,593
But I, on the other hand,
would like to help you, Mokuba.

42
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:52,820
Let me be honest with you.

43
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:56,264
I can see that you're
different from the others.

44
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,597
So I'll save you.

45
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:01,500
save me but you're the
one who trapped me here

46
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:08,057
i didn't do anything i'm
your friend zetto is your

47
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:11,757
enemy not me i am the
only one in this world you

48
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:16,297
can trust mokuba you're
the only one i can trust

49
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:21,040
awesome kaiba crushed the
last member of the Big five.

50
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:22,720
Well, Zeto.

51
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:24,660
Well, what?

52
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:30,099
You may have won your duel, but
you've lost something more important.

53
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:31,340
Your brother.

54
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:33,080
Where is he?

55
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:35,540
Here's a hint. Just look down.

56
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:37,320
The road's back.

57
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:40,420
Proceed ahead and you may find him.

58
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,230
Mokuba!

59
00:03:42,540 --> 00:03:43,840
I'm on my way!

60
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:45,520
Kaiba, come back!

61
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,838
That may be a trap!

62
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,880
Just stay out of this, Yugi. What?

63
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:52,577
Who do you think you are?

64
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:54,660
This doesn't concern you, Wheeler.

65
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:56,180
It's family business.

66
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:00,480
Okay, fine.

67
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:03,700
Lose your body for all we
care, you stuck-up jerk.

68
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:04,720
Who needs him?

69
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,177
We're better off without
him anyway, right, Yugi?

70
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:09,340
Goodbye and good riddance, Kaiba.

71
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,820
Hold on, guys.

72
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,980
We should help him save Mokuba.

73
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:17,857
Yeah, and if he finds Noah, then
he might find my body. He's right.

74
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:20,999
Following Kaiba may be the
only way to save Tristan.

75
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:21,970
Hallelujah!

76
00:04:22,053 --> 00:04:22,897
Did you hear that?

77
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:24,500
Thank you, Serenity.

78
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:27,840
I knew you'd believe it's
really me trapped in here.

79
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,960
I can always count on you.

80
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:33,180
For all we know, you're Noah's pet baboon.

81
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:37,800
We can't let Kaiba go alone.

82
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:39,700
I'm going to go after him.

83
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:41,680
Hey, Yugi, wait!

84
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:42,940
I'm going too.

85
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:44,840
Ah, give me a break.

86
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,550
Great.

87
00:04:46,633 --> 00:04:48,097
So now what are we gonna do?

88
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:51,180
We're gonna go in there
and help Kaiba find Mokuba.

89
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:52,440
No can do, sis.

90
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:56,153
I'm sick of helping Kaiba and
not getting any thank yous.

91
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:57,280
I'm with you.

92
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:01,040
If we were in trouble, Kaiba
would never go in after us.

93
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:05,120
Well, guys, suit yourself. Hey, stop.

94
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:06,677
I can't believe this.

95
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,477
Even my own sister won't listen to me.

96
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,020
All right, I'm going in.

97
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,540
Aw, come on!

98
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:14,880
Can't we talk about this?

99
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:18,700
Oh, the tunnel!

100
00:05:18,940 --> 00:05:19,820
It's gone!

101
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:23,180
Yugi! Hey-ya!

102
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:27,000
I'm coming, Mokuma!

103
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:30,730
Great.

104
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:33,351
I should have known this wouldn't be easy.

105
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:35,980
I'm tired of your tricks, Noah.

106
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:43,160
Seto, help me! Mokuba!

107
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:47,940
Mokuba, is that you over there?

108
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:53,650
Seto.

109
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,430
Mokuba!

110
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:03,260
Noah, what have you done with him?

111
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:09,530
Great.

112
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:11,560
Want to flip a coin? Nope.

113
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:12,860
He went this way.

114
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:15,860
Taya, you sure about that?

115
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:18,440
I have absolutely no idea.

116
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,460
That makes two of us.

117
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:23,380
Slow down, Taya.

118
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:26,132
Your legs are longer than mine, remember?

119
00:06:29,060 --> 00:06:30,760
Hey, check it out, Yugi.

120
00:06:31,580 --> 00:06:33,137
Yeah, there's a light ahead.

121
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:35,691
I hope that means we chose the right path.

122
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:38,000
Well, we're about to find out.

123
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:45,817
Oh, it's some kind of an
old mansion or something.

124
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:46,860
Really old.

125
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,380
Be careful, Yugi.

126
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:55,377
Whatever this place is, someone
doesn't want us going in there.

127
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:56,700
But I wonder why.

128
00:06:57,700 --> 00:07:00,440
Hey, do you hear what I hear? Huh?

129
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,640
It sounds like crying.

130
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,780
Yeah, I do hear it.

131
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:06,817
It's a baby.

132
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,380
Maybe that's some kind of virtual nursery.

133
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:13,200
Or what if that baby is all alone?

134
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:16,020
We've got to get in there and find out.

135
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:29,460
My patience is growing thin.

136
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,757
Waiting is not something I enjoy.

137
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:37,637
I must obtain Little
Yugi's Millennium Puzzle

138
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:40,460
and the two remaining Egyptian God Cards.

139
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:44,820
It's time I took matters
into my own hands again.

140
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:48,420
Is it me, or did it just get foggy?

141
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:51,420
Looks like fog to me.

142
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:56,280
Well, the virtual fun
never ends in this place.

143
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:58,250
Yeah.

144
00:07:58,333 --> 00:08:01,662
I'm just dying to see what surprise
Noah has in store for us next.

145
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:12,720
Ah, thanks for dropping in, Seto.

146
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,220
Noah, where's my little brother?

147
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:20,220
I demand that you bring him. Okuba.

148
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:26,100
See, Seto, your little brother
is safe and sound thanks to me.

149
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:29,197
You're the one who took him
from me in the first place,

150
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:32,217
so I don't know what kind of
stunt you're trying to pull.

151
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:33,418
Just hand him over.

152
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,740
Don't you remember?

153
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:41,340
It was your ex-employee Nesbitt
disguised as Tristan who took Mokuba.

154
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:44,665
Maybe you should have
been a better boss, Seto.

155
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:48,380
Anyway, it was me who saved
Mokuba from the Big Five.

156
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:50,440
You should be thanking me.

157
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,620
Come on, Mokuba. Let's go.

158
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,030
No!

159
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:56,414
What's wrong with you?

160
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,129
We're getting out of here.

161
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,280
Right now.

162
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,480
Go without me!

163
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:03,460
I'm staying right here.

164
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:08,046
You just stood there and watched
while they took me away, Seto.

165
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,290
I what?

166
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:12,880
Noah, what did you say to my brother?

167
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:16,280
What kind of lies did you
poison his brain with?

168
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:18,220
Not one, Seto.

169
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:22,380
Mokuba realized how little you
care about him all by himself.

170
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:25,940
So maybe you should take
his advice and just go.

171
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,880
Snap out of it, Mokuba.

172
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:29,590
Oh,

173
00:09:29,673 --> 00:09:31,637
it'll take more than
shouting to erase all of

174
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:34,337
those painful memories
from your brother's mind,

175
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:35,250
Seto.

176
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:37,917
Think of all those times
you abandoned him just

177
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,588
so you could achieve
your own selfish goals.

178
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,380
That's a lie!

179
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,720
I've never treated Mokuba like that!

180
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:46,620
Must you raise your voice?

181
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,420
Mokuba, please!

182
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:50,380
Don't listen to Noah's lies!

183
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:52,405
He's trying to drive us apart!

184
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,460
You've done enough. It's okay.

185
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:58,900
I won't let him hurt
you anymore. Let's go.

186
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,300
Get back here!

187
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:03,500
Hey, this is not one of
your sick games, Noah.

188
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:06,760
You will not destroy
the only family I have.

189
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:12,237
You have no family.

190
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,880
You're all alone now.

191
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:17,580
It seems to me that Mokuba
would rather be my brother.

192
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:21,437
And he's not the only thing
I'll take from you. Enough!

193
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:26,160
As far as I'm concerned, you don't
deserve anything that you have now.

194
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:30,580
So, I'll make sure your
possessions go to someone who does.

195
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:34,080
And who deserves to have what's mine?

196
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,040
Me, of course.

197
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:43,177
Taya, I still hear it, but
there's not a baby in sight.

198
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:44,297
And it's getting louder.

199
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:45,277
Let's go that way.

200
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:48,066
It's got to be coming
from one of these rooms.

201
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:52,060
No babies in here

202
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:59,100
Another empty room This place
seems to be deserted Weird

203
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:03,000
Hey, I found something It's a rattle

204
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:06,717
I'd be crying too If I were stuck in a

205
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:09,506
creepy old house With
no rattle You know what,

206
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:13,247
I don't think there's really a
baby In this place at all, Taya

207
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:17,057
Then who's crying Unless
it's just a digital sound

208
00:11:17,140 --> 00:11:21,020
file that's part of Noah's
freaky virtual universe! Exactly!

209
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:23,610
Huh?

210
00:11:23,693 --> 00:11:24,680
Check it out, Taya!

211
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:26,857
It looks like a picture of someone!

212
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:28,822
This might tell us where we are!

213
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,784
So who's in the snapshot, Yugi?

214
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,900
This is weird! What is?

215
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:40,480
What are all these contraptions?

216
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:43,180
And where are those fools?

217
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:45,780
What's this?

218
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:47,820
Well, well.

219
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:51,220
A locked door is always
a good place to begin.

220
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:55,580
You have entered an invalid password.

221
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:56,900
Entrance denied.

222
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:58,410
What?

223
00:11:58,493 --> 00:12:00,360
I have no patience for this.

224
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:02,180
I won't be stopped.

225
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:05,240
I'll find you, Yugi.

226
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:07,820
All right.

227
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:12,258
Being trapped in the body of a robot
monkey is not as fun as it looks.

228
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:17,437
Guys, what's got eight
eyes and lives underwater?

229
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:18,402
Is that a joke?

230
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:21,297
We're not exactly in the
mood for laughs, Chimp Boy.

231
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:24,337
There's something down there I think
you guys might want to look at.

232
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:25,600
And there I was,

233
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:30,465
thinking you couldn't get any more annoying
than you already were, Banana Breath.

234
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,860
First of all, hands up for here!

235
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,980
You have got to chill out! What?

236
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,720
Did you say chill?

237
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:39,797
Why don't you take a
look down there first?

238
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,097
The little monkey's scared.

239
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:43,657
I'll give you something
to be scared about.

240
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:45,858
It's my double monkey noogie attack.

241
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:51,480
What is that thing?

242
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:56,280
No way.

243
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:57,972
It's four at a big five.

244
00:12:58,180 --> 00:13:00,827
We beat you freaks of
nature fair and square.

245
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:04,511
But we still have some unfinished
business to take care of.

246
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:07,700
What do you creeps want from us? Simple.

247
00:13:07,980 --> 00:13:09,817
The same thing we've always wanted.

248
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,120
Your bodies!

249
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:12,482
Now what, Joey?

250
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:14,140
Don't worry, sis.

251
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:18,037
This bunch of wackos couldn't
duel their way out of a paper bag.

252
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:20,532
What makes you think we want to duel you?

253
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:23,240
My associates and I have had enough gains.

254
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,678
Now it's time for us to take action.

255
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,010
How's that?

256
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:30,760
Why duel you when we can
take your bodies by force?

257
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:32,340
Now we have a problem.

258
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:37,519
This ought to keep these guys busy.

259
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:41,560
Ha ha ha ha! Ah!

260
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:48,180
Time to blow this taco stand.

261
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:53,140
What are you waiting for, man?

262
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:55,220
This thing won't start.

263
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:57,380
Come on, you piece of junk.

264
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:03,720
Didn't expect that from
the penguin, did ya?

265
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,860
Witness dismissed.

266
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:12,560
Oh, Joey.

267
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:14,800
I'm trying my best.

268
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:17,820
Start your rust bucket. Come on.

269
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:21,220
It's starting.

270
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:22,600
Let's roll.

271
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:25,717
Warn me when you're going to do that.

272
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:27,600
I'm not wearing a seat belt.

273
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:33,760
It's time you learn the truth. What truth?

274
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:40,357
Take a close look at
the virtual projection

275
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:42,980
in front of you It's you and my stepfather

276
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:50,220
Yes, he and I have a history as well
It's Noah and Kaiba But what's going on?

277
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:54,788
Does this thing mean
anything to you, Kaiba?

278
00:14:56,680 --> 00:15:02,320
It's a trick This is a picture of my
stepfather Your stepdad? With Noah?

279
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:04,820
Pay attention to the show, Seto.

280
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:07,373
I think it will clear things up for you.

281
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:13,780
Who's this kid?

282
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:15,980
He is my latest acquisition.

283
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:20,517
His name is Seto, and he and his
brother will be coming to live with us.

284
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,188
He's extremely intelligent.

285
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:25,720
You could learn a lot from
him, and that's my plan.

286
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:28,757
Seto will be here to
constantly challenge you.

287
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,297
My hope is that having
him around the house

288
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:33,851
will motivate you to improve your studies.

289
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:38,280
After all, if I'm going to hand
Kyber Corp over to you someday, Noah,

290
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:40,677
you'll have to prove
to me that you have the

291
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:43,936
intellect it takes to run a
company of this magnitude.

292
00:15:45,020 --> 00:15:45,850
All right.

293
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:48,040
You won't be disappointed, father.

294
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:50,937
What did he say?

295
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,140
That's his dad!

296
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:56,560
Not quite what you were
expecting, is it, Seto?

297
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,040
You and I being stepbrothers.

298
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,540
But it's all true.

299
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:03,140
I am Gozaburo's one true son.

300
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:06,057
And I was always supposed
to inherit his empire.

301
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:08,797
You were nothing but another
one of my father's servants.

302
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:10,409
Brought in to motivate me.

303
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:15,037
That's the only reason my father let
Riff Raff like you into his house.

304
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,160
To train me.

305
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:19,017
And that's the story of how an orphan with

306
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:22,340
no class became the
president of Kaiba Corp.

307
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:23,780
Not true.

308
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,157
Oh, it's true.

309
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:29,097
And now the time has finally
arrived for me to reclaim

310
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:32,460
my rightful position as the
head of my father's empire.

311
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:36,100
Sorry, I guess this means
that you're out of a job.

312
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:39,320
Noah, your story makes no sense.

313
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:43,776
If you're really Gozaburo's son, how
is it that I never met you before?

314
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:45,060
Answer that, Noah!

315
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,840
Well, that's part two of my story.

316
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:52,200
Alert, alert, alert, alert.

317
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:53,400
Oh no!

318
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:56,837
Sorry, but I have to cut this short.

319
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:57,750
Don't move.

320
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:00,140
I'll be back after I deal with them.

321
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,780
You're staying here, understand?

322
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,360
The rest of the gang's in trouble!

323
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:09,420
They're gaining on us! Joey!

324
00:17:10,220 --> 00:17:11,220
Be careful!

325
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:19,120
Dude, straight ahead!

326
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:20,634
These guys won't quit!

327
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:21,896
There's another one!

328
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:24,680
I've got you now!

329
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:34,780
Are you still in one piece, Duke?

330
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:39,060
I think so. Serenity! I'm okay.

331
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,540
For now, maybe.

332
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:44,880
But soon all of your
bodies will belong to us!

333
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:51,020
Now, which of you two should I
choose to take control of? Hold on.

334
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:53,457
I want to have first choice, Lector.

335
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:55,481
We're going in size order, Crump.

336
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:56,960
So you choose last.

337
00:17:57,420 --> 00:17:59,697
That's the most ridiculous
thing I've ever heard.

338
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:01,133
I'm choosing right now.

339
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:04,260
Keep your wings to
yourself until I say so.

340
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:05,300
Stop it, fools.

341
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:10,460
We don't have time for all this bickering.

342
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:12,880
Choose a body and stick with it.

343
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:15,080
Then let me go first. Enough!

344
00:18:15,420 --> 00:18:16,420
Calm yourself.

345
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:21,480
We have to act quickly if we want to
escape into the real world. What's that?

346
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:22,990
Huh?

347
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:24,620
Attention, fool.

348
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:26,200
This game is over.

349
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:30,820
Master Noah, it's not what
it looks like. Really?

350
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:33,220
So you're not breaking my rules?

351
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:35,680
What kind of fool do you take me for?

352
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:38,120
Please, I can explain, Noah.

353
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:42,017
I gave you all the chance to win
your freedom and you all failed.

354
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:43,660
Now you'll pay the price.

355
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:54,340
Gentlemen, you're all dismissed.

356
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:57,800
No one disobeys my rules
and gets away with it.

357
00:18:58,260 --> 00:18:59,220
Oh, man.

358
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,384
Hey, you all right there, Duke?

359
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:05,280
Yeah, I've never been better. Hey, guys!

360
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,540
We found you!

361
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,220
Is everyone all right?

362
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,380
We're all fine.

363
00:19:12,100 --> 00:19:12,930
Awesome!

364
00:19:13,013 --> 00:19:14,517
That's the best news I've heard all day!

365
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,760
Those whips never stood a chance.

366
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:19,540
I guess the action never stopped.

367
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:21,033
You can say that again.

368
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:25,400
This just doesn't add up. Kaiba?

369
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:30,968
Could Noah's story about you being his
long-lost stepbrother actually be true?

370
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:36,400
Noah's story is nothing but one big lie
designed to mess with my head, Yugi.

371
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:39,497
The supposed conversation
he had with Gozaburo

372
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:41,874
would have happened over six years ago.

373
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:45,540
Which is when this was taken,
based on the imprinted date.

374
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:48,660
But look closely.

375
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:52,380
Noah looks the same as he does now.

376
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,640
He hasn't aged in six years?

377
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:05,570
Yama!
